OL,3,GNEWSA'My dad never forgot that one
OL,4,Ateacher's moment of kindness'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs a young boy John Richardson loved
OL,7,Fnothing more than looking for rabbits
OL,8,Fin the fields behind his school in
OL,9,FThurnscoe. But, aged four, it was only
OL,10,Fpossible with the help of a teacher
OL,11,Fguiding him through the long grass.
OL,13,FNow, more than 80 years later, he has
OL,14,Frepaid that simple act of kindness by
OL,15,Fleaving #8,000 to the school in his
OL,16,Fwill, following his death aged 86.
OL,18,FHis daughter Kate Davis said the
OL,19,F"warmth and kindness" shown to her
OL,20,Ffather had stayed with him through his
OL,21,Flife and was something he had chatted
OL,22,Fto her about before he died.
